From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:22:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add dual-VLAN DSA offload

Model service and customer VLAN tags independently so an RTL837x private
802.1ad source-port tag can coexist with a customer VLAN. Preserve DSA
identity tags on punted traffic; otherwise ARP and DHCP frames lose their
source-port identity after the first accelerated flow.

Initialize the ingress, EDMA, tunnel and egress TPID registers with the
same 802.1Q/802.1ad definition used by QSDK. Let device-tree mark DSA
conduits which always carry a service tag as persistent QinQ core ports;
flow references inherit that baseline instead of changing shared parsing
state while DHCP or PPPoE control traffic is active.

Keep transient ingress and egress QinQ port roles independently
refcounted. An ingress classifier owns only the ingress role, while a
destination flow owns its egress role. Program all shared resources
transactionally and quarantine a slot when hardware cleanup fails.

Record PPPoE topology at PPP_CHANNEL_CONNECT but defer VLAN, L3 and
session table programming until the first eligible IP flow. The notifier
fires before LCP/IPCP, so activating PPE there can consume PPPoE control
packets before negotiation finishes. Retain the activated hierarchy across
flow lifetime and release it at disconnect.

Limit fallback egress tag insertion to absent tag slots and expose the live
TPIDs, port roles and raw VLAN translation rows through debugfs.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
